Objectives
Demonstrate how Google Cloud Pub/Sub facilitates real-time messaging and
communication between distributed applications by:
1.Creating a Pub/Sub topic
2.Creating a subscription
3.Publishing messages to the topic
4.Receiving messages from the subscription

Step 1: Enable Pub/Sub API
Before using Pub/Sub, enable its API:

gcloud services enable pubsub.googleapis.com

Step 2: Create a Pub/Sub Topic
gcloud pubsub topics create my-topic

Step 3: Create a Subscription
gcloud pubsub subscriptions create my-subscription --topic=my-topic

● Messages published to my-topic will be delivered to
my-subscription.

Step 4: Publish a Message
Send a test message to the topic:

gcloud pubsub topics publish my-topic --message="Hello, Pub/Sub!"

Step 5: Receive Messages
Fetch messages from the subscription:

gcloud pubsub subscriptions pull my-subscription
--auto-ack

● --auto-ack: Acknowledges message receipt, so it is removed
from the queue.

Step 6: Simulate Real-Time Messaging
Run the following commands in two separate terminals:
Terminal 1: Continuous Subscriber (Listening)

gcloud pubsub subscriptions pull my-subscription --auto-ack --limit=10

Terminal 2: Publisher (Sending Messages)
gcloud pubsub topics publish my-topic --message="Message 1"
gcloud pubsub topics publish my-topic --message="Message 2"

Step 7: Clean Up Resources
To avoid billing charges, delete the topic and subscription:

gcloud pubsub subscriptions delete my-subscription

gcloud pubsub topics delete my-topic
